{"ref":"BDB, דָּֽרְיָ֫וֶשׁ","hw":"דָּֽרְיָ֫וֶשׁ","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">דָּֽרְיָ֫וֶשׁ</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m. Darius (</strong>Old Pers. <em>Dârayavaʾush</em> cf. Spieg<sup>APK 81</sup><strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>1.</strong>  Darius Hystaspis, 522–485 <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:5\" href=\"/Ezra.4.5\">Ezr 4:5</a> <a data-ref=\"Haggai 1:1\" href=\"/Haggai.1.1\">Hg 1:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Haggai 1:15\" href=\"/Haggai.1.15\">15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Haggai 2:10\" href=\"/Haggai.2.10\">2:10</a> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 1:1\" href=\"/Zechariah.1.1\">Zc 1:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 1:7\" href=\"/Zechariah.1.7\">7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 7:1\" href=\"/Zechariah.7.1\">7:1</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  Darius Codomannus, 336–332 <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 12:22\" href=\"/Nehemiah.12.22\">Ne 12:22</a>.<br><strong>3.</strong>  ‘Darius the Mede,’ <a data-ref=\"Daniel 9:1\" href=\"/Daniel.9.1\">Dn 9:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 11:1\" href=\"/Daniel.11.1\">11:1</a>, cf. Bev <sup>Dan. p. 19</sup>.","next":"BDB, דַּרְיוֹשׁ","prev":"BDB, דָּרוֹם"}